      "content": "The legal precedents overwhelmingly show that the invocation of executive privilege is frequently weaponized to shield political malfeasance, not just protect state secrets. When the privilege is used to obstruct legitimate investigations into misconduct, it ceases to be a constitutional necessity and becomes an abuse of power. Therefore, the argument for maintaining strong congressional oversight is objectively grounded in the foundational principle that no branch of government is above the law.",
